This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ If the return value is negative, new list doesnt contain x". It is referring to the Count contract test where we check if the count of the array list is negative which is not possible so this statement should always be true.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(arrList.Capacity >= arrList.Count);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ Old size of array list equals to new size of array list after adding or removing". It is referring to the Add and Remove contract tests where we want to ensure that the size of the array list stays the same or increases after adding elements and decreases after removing elements.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(arrList[index] == x);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ The new array list contains x at its new position". This statement would be true if the PUT_SetContract test successfully updated the array list at the specified index with the new value.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(arrList.Capacity >= arrList.Count);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ The array list capacity equals or exceeds the number of elements". Once we add an element to the ArrayList, the capacity should increase if necessary to accommodate the new element.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ New array list count equals old array list count plus one". This assertion test the CountContract test case. This indicates that after an element has been added, the count of the array list should increase by one.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ New count of array list equals old count of array list after adding an element". It is referring to the Count contract test case for the scenario after successful addition of an element.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount + 1);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ Old count of array list equals new count of array list after removing an element". This assertion tests the Remove contract test case. This would be true if an element was successfully removed from the array list, and the count of the array list decreased by one.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_index);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ Get value at old index equals to old index". The assertion tests the Get Contract test case where it checks if value at old index is same as old index just before changing its value.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(New_Ret == Old_arrListCount - 1);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ New count of array list equals old count of array list minus one". This is a pre condition for removing contract, here we tell Pex that after removing an element the count should decrease by one.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX);
</code>
This code block was generated from the comment "@@@ New array list contains X equal to old array list contains X". This test case is checking if after removing (if X was in list before removal) X remains in the list.
<code>
    Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX);
</code>
